 "headline": "ADWIN refit 1 times vs FIXED 14 on 285 identical test dates; ADWIN - FIXED IC +0.0085 (t 1.567, p 0.1183); 264 dates ran on a stale model, max age 13 months; fit seconds 0.93 vs 25.52",
 "verdict": "ADWIN NEVER FIRED after the mandatory first fit, so the ADWIN arm is one model carried across every test month (max age 13 months). That is a fact about the ERROR STREAM -- at this scale it is stationary to the detector -- and only secondarily about the cadence. Read the stale-vs-fresh IC split, not the refit count: a monthly refit that changes nothing is ceremony, and a detector that cannot see the drift is not evidence there is none.",
